---
title: LSASS Credential Dumping via comsvcs.dll MiniDump
id: 9e2f3a4b-5c6d-4e8f-a7b8-0c1d2e3f4a01
status: experimental
description: Detects invocation of the legitimate comsvcs.dll MiniDump export against the LSASS process, a living-off-the-land credential dumping technique documented in Volt Typhoon intrusions that avoids deploying separate dumping malware.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-144a
tags:
    - attack.credential_access
    - attack.t1003.001
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        Image|endswith: '\rundll32.exe'
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'comsvcs.dll'
            - 'MiniDump'
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate diagnostic memory dump collected by IT/support staff using this documented technique
level: critical

---
title: Exploitation Attempt Against End-of-Life Edge Device Management Interface
id: 9e2f3a4b-5c6d-4e8f-a7b8-0c1d2e3f4a02
status: experimental
description: Detects inbound requests to the administrative interface of a known end-of-life edge device (Fortinet, Ivanti, NETGEAR, Citrix, Cisco) exhibiting exploitation patterns, matching Volt Typhoon's primary initial access vector.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa24-038a
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1190
logsource:
    category: firewall
detection:
    selection:
        dst_port:
            - 443
            - 8443
            - 10443
        uri|contains:
            - '/remote/'
            - '/dana-na/'
            - '/+CSCOE+/'
    filter_patched_devices:
        dst_ip|cidr: 'PATCHED_DEVICE_INVENTORY'  # populate with confirmed patched/retired device IP ranges
    condition: selection and not filter_patched_devices
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate remote access to an unpatched-but-monitored device pending scheduled maintenance
level: high

