title: Authentication Originating from Residential or SOHO Proxy Infrastructure
id: 9e2f3a4b-5c6d-4e8f-a7b8-0c1d2e3f4a03
status: experimental
description: Detects successful authentication to corporate remote access or VPN services from IP space associated with residential ISPs or known compromised SOHO router infrastructure, matching Volt Typhoon's KV Botnet proxying technique used to obscure true traffic origin.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0035/
tags:
    - attack.command_and_control
    - attack.t1090.003
logsource:
    category: authentication
detection:
    selection:
        EventType: 'LoginSuccess'
        SourceIp|cidr: KV_BOTNET_PROXY_IOC_LIST  # populate via current threat intel feed
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate remote employee connecting from a home ISP that overlaps a stale IOC range
level: high

---
title: Self-Signed Certificate Matching KV Botnet Naming Pattern
id: 9e2f3a4b-5c6d-4e8f-a7b8-0c1d2e3f4a04
status: experimental
description: Detects TLS handshakes presenting a self-signed certificate with a common/subject name matching the "jdyfj"-style pattern reported in KV Botnet / JDY cluster infrastructure.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0035/
tags:
    - attack.command_and_control
    - attack.t1573
logsource:
    category: proxy
detection:
    selection:
        tls_cert_subject|re: 'jdyfj[a-z0-9]*'
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Coincidental certificate naming from an unrelated legitimate self-signed deployment
level: high

---
title: Exploratory Hands-on-Keyboard PowerShell Command Sequences
id: 9e2f3a4b-5c6d-4e8f-a7b8-0c1d2e3f4a05
status: experimental
description: Detects a pattern of repeated, incrementally-adjusted PowerShell commands from the same session inconsistent with a single scripted execution, matching Volt Typhoon's reported hands-on-keyboard, exploratory operating style.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-144a
tags:
    - attack.discovery
    - attack.t1059.001
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        Image|endswith: '\powershell.exe'
    condition: selection | count() by User, ParentProcessId > 15
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate administrator performing an extended interactive troubleshooting session
level: medium

---
title: Native LOLBin Discovery Commands Inconsistent with Admin Baseline
id: 9e2f3a4b-5c6d-4e8f-a7b8-0c1d2e3f4a06
status: experimental
description: Detects use of native Windows discovery utilities (net, ipconfig, netstat, systeminfo, wmic) chained together in a sequence outside normal administrative baselines, matching Volt Typhoon's near-total reliance on living-off-the-land tooling for discovery and lateral movement.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-144a
tags:
    - attack.discovery
    - attack.t1057
    - attack.t1082
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\net.exe'
            - '\ipconfig.exe'
            - '\netstat.exe'
            - '\systeminfo.exe'
            - '\wmic.exe'
    timeframe: 10m
    condition: selection | count() by User > 8
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate IT troubleshooting session running several discovery commands in sequence
level: low

---
title: Authentication Targeting Personal Webmail from Corporate-Managed Device
id: 9e2f3a4b-5c6d-4e8f-a7b8-0c1d2e3f4a07
status: experimental
description: Detects a managed IT/network administrator endpoint authenticating to a personal (non-corporate) webmail provider, consistent with Volt Typhoon's reported technique of targeting IT staff's personal email to evade corporate monitoring.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa24-038a
tags:
    - attack.discovery
    - attack.t1589
logsource:
    category: proxy
detection:
    selection:
        c-uri|contains:
            - 'mail.google.com'
            - 'outlook.live.com'
            - 'mail.yahoo.com'
    filter_it_hosts:
        src_hostname|contains: 'IT_ADMIN_HOSTGROUP'  # populate with IT/network admin workstation inventory
    condition: selection and filter_it_hosts
falsepositives:
    - IT staff member legitimately checking personal email on a managed device during a break
level: low

---
title: Long-Retention Auth Log Gap Suggesting Silent Session Persistence
id: 9e2f3a4b-5c6d-4e8f-a7b8-0c1d2e3f4a08
status: experimental
description: Detects a valid account maintaining an active authenticated session across an unusually long duration without corresponding periodic re-authentication events, consistent with Volt Typhoon's long-term, low-visibility pre-positioning objective rather than immediate collection.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa24-038a
tags:
    - attack.persistence
    - attack.t1078
logsource:
    category: authentication
detection:
    selection:
        SessionDurationHours|gt: 72
        ReauthCount: 0
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate long-lived service account session under an accepted exception
level: low
